dogecoin.text:
@CryptoWhale I'm so lucky the guy who told me to get into Crypto said, "Either in a year you'll be a millionaire or 10 years."

I put 80% of my savings into Dogecoin in 2014...bought at the top and 2 weeks later I was down 70%. I HODL'd

3 years later I was up 7x my original $.

@yourmumscunt_ @sinequanun @ToughGoat @mrvalentinc @elonmusk I would not advise someone to go all in doge today since 1mil dogecoins cost $50k. I went all in when 1 million cost $500.

But that is legit a 100x return. Had I kept it in USD, that $500 would be worth $400 at best today. 

On a 5 year hold, you are better off in $DOGE.

@TheCryptoCPA I'd rather buy $400 worth of Dogecoin.

Year to date $DOGE has done 24x return. 
$BTC has done 3x return.

@XRPHuey @CanteringClark I've been in crypto since 2014 when I had a choice....1 $BTC for $600 or 1 million $DOGE for $500. I chose Dogecoin.

Today 1 $BTC is $63000
1 million $DOGE is $130000

@MHurkie @Mikey_Mach @crypto_bitlord7 $DOGE was half a cent Jan 1st. Today Dogecoin is 31 cents.

That's 60x growth YTD. BTC did 3x growth same timeframe. 

We're not even half way through the crypto bull market.

@TheCryptoDog Link is my biggest bag. Doge was 2% my holdings...now it's 40%.

That's why Dogecoin survives. Those who's first coin was $DOGE always keep some and then the next bull market it moons, and we remember, "Oh yeah, it always moons."

Then we forget until the next bull cycle.

@debostic Does @ScottAdamsSays have a name for the positive version of a linguistic kill shot?

@elonmusk calling $DOGE "The People's Crypto" was that. It stuck and has brought nothing but good to Dogecoin.

And may turn into a kill shot for $BTC.

@CryptoWhale @mcuban @elonmusk @TDogewhisperer @spair @itsALLrisky In 2014 one $BTC cost $600 and 1 million $DOGE cost $500.

Today 1 $BTC is $36k and 1 million $DOGE is $310k.

No future where 1 Doge isn't $1.
